From b839c0a14f1b1fb4888e05e68c6a282d409d46dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 13:24:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(runtime): precondition finalizer removal on the object
 uid

The removal patch tested only `/metadata/finalizers/<index>` for our own name. That
name is identical across incarnations, so an object deleted, recreated under the same
name and re-finalized between the `Cleanup` await and the patch would have the *new*
object's finalizer removed - releasing a hold whose cleanup never ran, which is the one
outcome finalizers exist to prevent. The patch now also tests `/metadata/uid` when the
object has one, pinning the removal to the object cleanup was run for. The index test is
kept, and objects without a uid patch exactly as before.

Patch construction moves into two pure functions so it can be asserted without a server:
`finalizer.rs` had no tests at all, and both `Test` operations were unexercised. Adds four
unit tests over the built patches - the removal patch with and without a uid, and both add
shapes, unchanged.

Also states in the doc comment the two exits from a stuck delete (restore the controller,
or strip the finalizer by hand and accept the leak), which the caveat named neither of.

No public API or behaviour change beyond the added precondition.

Written by an ai-registry intake run as a task row against the source tree; not a PR.

Signed-off-by: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
